There is something genuinely interesting in that observation, though I'd separate the cultural joke from the engineering constraint.
What QS is doing requires you to be indifferent to vendor boundaries at the application layer. GPT doesn't care that Gemini is owned by Google. Gemini doesn't care that DeepSeek is DeepSeek. QS treats all three as nodes with observable state and an input/output interface.
